\ul Extends\par
\ulnone Q.4  Explain the concept of inheritance in OOP and how it is implemented in PHP.\par
ans.4    Concept of Inheritance in Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)\par
Inheritance is one of the core principles of Object-Oriented Programming (OOP).\par
It allows a class (called a child or subclass) to inherit properties and methods from another class (called a parent or base class).\par
This promotes code reusability, extensibility, and a hierarchical class structure.\par
\f3\u9881?\u-497? Key Points\par
The child class gets access to all public and protected members of the parent class.\par
The child can:\par
Use inherited properties/methods directly.\par
Override methods from the parent class.\par
Add its own new properties and methods.\par
The private members of the parent class are not accessible directly by the child class.\par
\u-10179?\u-9029? Implementation in PHP\par
PHP supports single inheritance, meaning a class can only inherit from one parent class (though it can use traits to include behavior from multiple sources).\par
Example:\par
<?php\par
// Parent class\par
class Animal \{\par
    public $name;\par
\f4     \f3  public function __construct($name) \{\par
        $this->name = $name;\par
    \}\par
\f4         \f3 public function speak() \{\par
        echo "$this->name makes a sound.";\par
    \}\par
\}\par
// Child class inheriting from Animal\par
class Dog extends Animal \{\par
\f4      \f3  // Overriding parent method\par
    public function speak() \{\par
        echo "$this->name barks!";\par
    \}\par
\f4     \f3  // New method specific to Dog\par
    public function fetch() \{\par
        echo "$this->name is fetching the ball.";\par
    \}\par
\}\par
// Creating an object of the child class\par
$dog = new Dog("Buddy");\par
$dog->speak();  // Output: Buddy barks!\par
$dog->fetch();  // Output: Buddy is fetching the ball.\par
?>\par
\u-10178?\u-8727? Explanation\par
class Dog extends Animal \f5\emdash  the Dog class inherits from the Animal class.\par
The constructor and speak() method are defined in Animal.\par
The Dog class:\par
Overrides the speak() method.\par
Adds a new method fetch().\par
When we create a Dog object, it can use both:\par
Inherited properties/methods ($name, constructor)\par
Its own methods (fetch())\f0   \par
\par
