Using parent:: Keyword\par
The parent:: keyword allows a child class to access methods or constructors from its parent:\par
class Cat extends Animal \{\par
    public function __construct($name) \{\par
        parent::__construct($name); // Call parent constructor\par
    \}\par
          public function speak() \{\par
        parent::speak(); // Call parent method\par
        echo " And $this->name meows.";\par
    \}\par
\}\par
